      "settings": {
        "eyebrow_text": "The problem it solves",
        "heading": "<p>Connection is hard to feel. LINK ONE makes it obvious.</p>",
        "copy": "<p>If your arms cast early and the body never catches up, the swing looks athletic and still hits soft. LINK ONE gives you a physical cue when that disconnect starts — so you can rebuild the link on the next swing.</p>",
        "ritual_heading": "A simple 5-minute drill",
        "note": "Go slow. You’re training connection, not speed.",
        "panel_eyebrow": "Quick read",
        "panel_title": "Keep the arms linked to the turn.",
        "panel_copy": "Think of the swing as arms and body moving as one piece. When they separate, you’ll feel it. When they stay together, the belt stays quiet.",
